at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2025-02-07T16:33:01Z","updated_at":"2025-02-07T19:04:10Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nTested in: 4.3, 4.4beta2\n\n### System information\n\nUbuntu 20.04\n\n### Issue description\n\nInstanciating a scene using SkeletonModifications multiple times will cause the older scenes to behave unexpectedly. It seems to cause the target nodes of Modifications like Look-At and Inverse-Kinematik to change to the one of the newest instance for all instances.\nThat's despite the property using a NodePath, which implies that the Modification-Resource isn't supposed to hold a reference to the actual Node.\n\nSetting both the ModificationStack and the Modification to local_to_scene fixes the issue.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nthe MRP will spawn a simple Inverse Kinematic Arm multiple times. on each new spawn the previous arms will seemingly change their target to the target of the new one.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[skeleton-modification-instances.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/18709366/skeleton-modification-instances.zip)","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102541/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102541/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}